WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
Let u be odd and greater than one.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.520
The all-ones polynomial
J has u squared terms.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:13.060
Substitute P equal to one: every power
becomes one, so J of one equals u squared.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.920
For u equal to three, count nine
ones before taking any residue.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.740
Now use the same nonzero
characteristic-two quotient ring as

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.560
before. Two equals the product
of one plus i and one minus i,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.700
so a pair of ones reduces to zero.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.200
In the residue calculation, pair
eight of the nine ones; one remains.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.680
In general, u squared is odd, so J of
one has residue one modulo one plus i.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.480
Our sum contains J of one divided by c of
one, so account for the denominator too.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.940
The polynomial c has
real integer coefficients

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.640
and satisfies c times c
star equals u squared.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.960
Star conjugates the coefficients
and reverses the powers.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.150
At P equal to one, every
reversed power is still one,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.040
and conjugating a real
coefficient leaves it unchanged.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.260
Thus c star of one equals c of one.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:15.100
The evaluated norm identity becomes
c of one squared equals u squared.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.140
Therefore c of one is
either u or negative u.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.660
The real-coefficient condition restricts
the value to these two real possibilities.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.280
Use the evaluation ring
with one over u adjoined.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.500
The denominator c of one, equal to
positive or negative u, is a unit there.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:36.640
Simplify the exact quotient before
reducing: J of one over c of one equals

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.540
u squared over positive or negative
u, giving positive or negative u.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.370
For u equal to three, nine
divided by three is three,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.000
and nine divided by negative three
is negative three. Now take residues.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.660
Since u is odd, its residue is one. Plus
and minus agree in characteristic two,

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.930
so either sign of the
quotient has residue one.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.680
The empty subset has input P equal
to one and positive alternating sign.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.980
Its normalized contribution,
including the unit denominator,

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.820
therefore has residue one
in the same common ring.
